# 🎯 Why This Is Useful

In real-world Spring applications, there can be hundreds of classes and objects.

Instead of manually creating and managing every object:

```java
new Alien();
new Laptop();
new Student();
new Employee();
```

Spring can manage these objects through its IoC Container.

This helps achieve:

* Loose coupling
* Centralized object management
* Dependency Injection
* Easier maintenance
* Better testability
* Cleaner application architecture

